2) give a short explanation why you gave that score, based on the rubric. **This part will be graded partially based on completeness, and partially based on whether you implemented the rubric correctly.** (For example, if the rubric prescribes a point deduction for a mistake that is in the exam, but you did not comment on this mistake, then we may deduct points. Similarly, if you deduct points for a mistake that is not in the exam, then we may deduct points.)

3) give a short discussion of what you think the strengths and weaknesses are of the AI-generated exam answers. **This part will be graded partially based on completeness, and partially based on the correctness of your justifications.** (For example, similar to the previous item, if you think something is a strength in the exam, but it is not correct given what we have discussed in class, then we may deduct points. Similarly, if you think something is a weakness when it is largely correct given what we have discussed in class, then we may deduct points.)

**Be sure to answer all questions, because (as stated above) we will be giving a lot of partial credit.**



